<header><p class="st-kicker">theocracy · Mesopotamia and Iran</p><h1 class="st-title">Islamic Republic of Iran</h1><p class="st-meta">1979 CE – present · capital Tehran</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Shia theocratic republic created by the revolution of 1979, in which elected institutions operate under the authority of a Supreme Leader.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Mass protests in 1978 brought down <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/pahlavi-iran">Pahlavi Iran</a>. Ayatollah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ruhollah-khomeini">Ruhollah Khomeini</a> returned from exile on 1 February 1979, and after a referendum the Islamic Republic was proclaimed on 1 April 1979. A constitution adopted in December 1979 enshrined velayat-e faqih, the guardianship of the Islamic jurist.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Power is shared between a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/supreme-leader-of-iran">Supreme Leader</a>, an elected president and parliament, and unelected bodies such as the Guardian Council and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islamic-revolutionary-guard-corps">Revolutionary Guards</a>. The early years saw the US embassy hostage crisis of 1979 to 1981, purges of leftists and liberals, and the Iran-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> War of 1980 to 1988. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-khamenei">Ali Khamenei</a> became Supreme Leader in 1989. Reformist periods under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mohammad-khatami">Mohammad Khatami</a> alternated with crackdowns, including on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iranian-green-movement">Green Movement</a> of 2009 and the 'Woman, Life, Freedom' protests of 2022.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>The country's nuclear programme led to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a>, the 2015 nuclear deal and the US withdrawal from it in 2018, and in 2025 to open war with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Israel</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran's</a> oil economy, regional alliances and internal dissent continue to shape the state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/islamic-republic-of-iran.jpg" alt="Islamic Republic of Iran" width="320" height="183"><figcaption>Image: SVG file: SiBr4Designer: Hamid NadimiConstruction: ISIRI · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Iran_(official).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1979 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>theocracy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Tehran</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ruhollah Khomeini, Ali Khamenei, Akbar Hashemi Rafsanjani</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Twelver Shia Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/iran">Iran</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Iran</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=2002&amp;focus=islamic-republic-of-iran" aria-label="Islamic Republic of Iran on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5978 888 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Islamic Republic of Iran lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6298 1144L6298 1144"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6298 1144h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6298 1144h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6298 1144h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Tehran. <a href="/atlas?year=2002&amp;focus=islamic-republic-of-iran">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
